+# Privacy by design
+
+## Data minimization
+- The site collects no personal data: no forms, cookies, storage, analytics, or logs with IPs.
+- `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` and a restrictive `Permissions-Policy` limit what the browser leaks or exposes.
+- Before adding any data collection, record the purpose, fields, retention, and legal basis here.
+
+## Third-party audit (2026-10-19)
+| Resource | Finding | Action |
+|---|---|---|
+| Hero image from `images.unsplash.com` | Leaked visitor IP/UA to a third party on every page load | Self-hosted at `assets/hero.jpg` |
+| Runtime dependencies | None (`server.js` uses Node built-ins only) | `pnpm dlx statikk` removed from `start` |
+
+Current third-party requests: **none**. CSP `default-src 'none'` makes the browser block any new one.
+`pnpm audit` (script `audit`) fails if an absolute URL appears in the HTML, so third-party resources get a deliberate review.
+Re-audit whenever a dependency or external resource is added, and at least yearly.
+
+## Secure data handling
+- HTTPS only (HSTS, `upgrade-insecure-requests`); server allows only GET/HEAD and serves an explicit allowlist of files (no path traversal).
+- Any future personal data: encrypt in transit and at rest, restrict access, set retention limits, support deletion.
+
+## Security headers
+Set in `server.js` and mirrored in `_headers` for static hosts: CSP, HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options,
+Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, COOP/COEP/CORP. Vulnerability reports: `/.well-known/security.txt`
+(placeholder contact/domain; replace before deploying).
+
+## Known gaps
+- CSP allows `'unsafe-inline'` styles because styles are inline in the HTML; move them to a CSS file to remove it.
+- The nav links to pages that don't exist yet (`/menu`, `/account`, etc.) and return 404.
